        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "add whatsapp outbound token diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOutbound WhatsApp direct sends can fail silently when WhatsApp Web needs trusted-contact token state or LID routing data for a recipient.\n\nAI-assisted: yes, Codex helped update this branch and evidence.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds outbound token diagnostics and LID-aware lookup paths around WhatsApp Web sends.\n\nThe send path now:\n\n- resolves phone-number targets through Baileys LID lookup and USync when possible\n- persists discovered PN/LID mappings for later sends\n- checks trusted-contact token state before direct sends\n- reports reachout timelock and new-chat quota diagnostics when a token is missing\n- keeps socket operations bounded by the existing WhatsApp socket timing wrapper\n- lets token-backed direct sends pass the monitor reachout-timelock gate\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers get clearer failures instead of accepted-but-undelivered direct WhatsApp sends, and already-known LID mappings are reused for later outbound messages.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `90e3f0c4c3f820c7da0fa8c0c60e9b3f2b99cf36`\n\nFocused validation on the current base:\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-whatsapp.config.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/send-api.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/socket-timing.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/monitor-inbox.behavior.test.ts\nTest Files  3 passed (3)\nTests       149 passed (149)\n```\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.extensions.test.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/extensions-test.tsbuildinfo\n# exit code 0\n```\n\n```text\n$ git diff --check\n# exit code 0\n```\n\n```text\n$ codex review --base origin/main\nNo actionable correctness, security, or maintainability regressions were found in the reviewed diff. Focused WhatsApp tests for the changed send API, socket timing, and monitor support passed.\n```\n\nBroader WhatsApp extension validation after the token-backed send fix:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm --config.verify-deps-before-run=false test:extension whatsapp\nTest Files  87 passed (87)\nTests       1040 passed (1040)\n```\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/monitor.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/send-api.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/send-api.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/socket-timing.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/socket-timing.test.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/monitor-inbox.test-harness.ts extensions/whatsapp/src/monitor-inbox.streams-inbound-messages.test-support.ts\n# exit code 0\n```\n",
